course: dictionary
lesson: 12682
title: Distrust
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Distrust means you cannot trust someone or something. You think they may lie to you or let you down. It can be a feeling (a noun) or an action (a verb, to distrust someone). «The villagers looked at the stranger with distrust.» The word with tells you the villagers did not trust him.
explain: Context clues help you work out distrust. «Mia broke her promise twice, so Sam began to distrust her.» The broken promises are the clue: Sam now thinks Mia may let him down again. Ask yourself, what would make someone not trust a person? The answer is close to the meaning.
explain: Distrust is a feeling, so it can be strong or weak. «There was deep distrust between the two families.» Deep shows the feeling is very strong. Distrust is the opposite of trust, so check by putting in not trust: if it still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
explain: Distrust can also be healthy. «Keep a healthy distrust of offers that seem too good to be true.» Being careful keeps you safe, so this is wise, not rude.
fact: Distrust means a feeling that you cannot trust someone or something.
fact: As a verb, «distrust» means to not trust someone: «I distrust the dog, because it growls at everyone.»
fact: As a noun, distrust has no plural, so we say «deep distrust», not «distrusts».
fact: Useful phrases are «with distrust», «a deep distrust of» and «mutual distrust», which means distrust on both sides.
fact: In history, mutual distrust between countries can lead to conflict. In online safety, a healthy distrust of strangers keeps you safe.
exercise: «The villagers eyed the stranger with distrust.» What does distrust mean here? | Hunger after a long walk | *A feeling that they could not trust him | Great love and friendship | Happy singing in the square
exercise: «Ben and Chloe had a deep distrust of each other, so neither would share a secret.» What does this suggest? | They had both lost their keys | *They did not trust each other | They were best friends | They were very hungry
exercise: Find the word that means to not trust someone. | *distrust | email | online | password
test: «A healthy distrust of strangers online keeps you safe.» Why is this healthy? | *Being careful protects you from people who may lie | It means you should be rude to everyone | Strangers are always honest | It means you have no friends
test: In «a deep distrust of heights», what kind of word is distrust? | *Noun | Verb | Adverb | Adjective
exam: Why might history books describe mutual distrust between two countries as dangerous? | Because it makes the countries famous | *Because it can lead to conflict | Because it means they are best friends | Because it helps crops grow
